<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Emotion> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Emotion Expression elements from the image. Emotion Expression includes: facial expressions, emotional gestures, mood indicators, affective elements, and emotional cues. For each emotional element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'mischievous_smile', 'concerned_expression'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the mischievous smile', 'the concerned expression'), 3) A brief description of the emotional state or expression. Focus on clearly visible emotional indicators that convey feelings or moods. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"mischievous_smile\", \"label\": \"the mischievous smile\", \"description\": \"A knowing, slightly devious smile suggesting mischief or satisfaction\"}"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#men_in_traditional_attire> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#reactingTo> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#text_overlay> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the scene depicted in the bottom half of the meme, where three men in traditional Middle Eastern attire are shown with exaggerated expressions of shock and amusement. The text overlay 'meanwhile at the isis strip club' explicitly frames this scene as the context for the user's imagined reaction, implying that the user is viewing or imagining this scenario. The user is not directly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the meme as a humorous, satirical, and offensive scenario invites the user to imagine themselves as part of the audience or as the observer of the absurd and degrading situation being portrayed. The projection is onto the 'isis_strip_club_scene' entity, which includes the men's reactions and the implied context of the text."@en .
