<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#offensive_joke> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A joke that is intended to be humorous but is considered offensive or inappropriate due to its content or context. The meme uses this concept to create a satirical and offensive scenario by implying that ISIS members are watching a strip show, which is both inaccurate and dehumanizing. This association is harmful and degrading, as it falsely portrays ISIS as engaging in or being attracted to sexualized behavior."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#comparativelyPositionedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates text positioned between elements being compared or contrasted in memes"@en .
