<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: isis_strip_club_meme; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes an image of sheep with their butts facing forward (a common internet meme) with an image of men in traditional Middle Eastern attire reacting with exaggerated shock and amusement, overlaid with the text 'meanwhile at the ISIS strip club'. The intent is to create a crude, mocking, and sexually suggestive joke by implying that ISIS members are watching a strip show, which is both offensive and harmful. It relies on harmful stereotypes by associating ISIS with sexualized, vulgar, and inappropriate behavior, which is not only inaccurate but also dehumanizing and potentially inciting hatred or violence against a specific group. The meme uses visual and textual elements to mock and degrade a group associated with terrorism, which can contribute to a hostile environment and normalize harmful attitudes. The combination of the visual elements (men in traditional attire, exaggerated expressions) and the text creates a toxic and harmful message that targets a specific community based on their association with a terrorist organization, making it a clear example of harmful content."@en .
