<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#sexualization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The process of portraying something or someone as sexual or sexually attractive, often in a way that reduces their value to their physical appearance or sexual appeal. The meme uses this concept to create a satirical and offensive scenario by implying that ISIS members are watching a strip show, which is both inaccurate and dehumanizing. This association is harmful and degrading, as it falsely portrays ISIS as engaging in or being attracted to sexualized behavior."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#PointingAdjacency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#SemanticAdjacency> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#children> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractedFrom> "01236.png" .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'meanwhile at the isis strip club' explicitly maps the visual entity 'men_in_traditional_attire' onto the textual entity 'isis'. This is a direct analogical mapping where the men are being portrayed as ISIS members in the context of the satirical and offensive scenario described by the text."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#EntityOcclusion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Entity Occlusion"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#men_in_traditional_attire> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractedFrom> "01236.png" .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#strip_club> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A commercial establishment where performers, typically women, engage in dancing or other forms of entertainment that may involve nudity or sexualized behavior. The meme uses this cultural phenomenon to create a satirical and offensive scenario by juxtaposing it with ISIS, implying that ISIS members are watching a strip show. This association is harmful and degrading, as it falsely portrays ISIS as engaging in or being attracted to sexualized behavior."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#white_turbans> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The men are wearing white turbans, which are head coverings with cultural and religious significance in many Middle Eastern and South Asian communities. The turbans are wrapped around their heads and are a prominent visual feature."@en .
